.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt RESCUE-STATIC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rescue-static
.Nd take the sealed disk's fixed address when no lease arrives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a shell script installed only in the recovery image, at
.Pa /bin/rescue-static .
It takes no arguments.
The recovery system's
.Pa /etc/network/interfaces
starts it in the background after starting the DHCP client for eth0,
with
.Ql post-up /bin/rescue-static &
under
.Ql iface eth0 inet dhcp .
.Pp
The script sleeps 25 seconds, then examines
.Ql ifconfig eth0 .
If the output does not contain
.Ql addr:0.0.0.0 ,
it exits with status 0 and no message.
Otherwise it reports:
.Dl rescue: no lease arrived; taking the fixed address
It reads the DHCP client's process ID from
.Pa /var/run/udhcpc.eth0.pid ,
sends SIGTERM, and waits up to ten seconds for the client to stop.
If the client does not stop, it reports:
.Dl rescue: the DHCP client will not stop; leaving the address alone
and exits with status 1.
.Pp
After the client stops, the script sets the address and default route:
.Dl ifconfig eth0 192.168.0.105 netmask 255.255.255.0
.Dl route add default gw 192.168.0.1
Failure of either command causes exit status 1.
On success it reports:
.Dl rescue: eth0: 192.168.0.105 through 192.168.0.1
All these messages go to standard error.
.Pp
A damaged boot partition can cause the machine to enter recovery
through the GRUB core image's own configuration.
On a network without DHCP, the fixed address permits SSH access
without someone choosing a menu entry at the keyboard.
The script stops the DHCP client first so a late lease cannot replace
the address during an SSH session.
.Pp
The address, mask, and gateway are the sealed disk's settings,
.Ql SEALED_ADDRESS ,
.Ql SEALED_MASK ,
and
.Ql SEALED_GATEWAY
in the source tree's
.Pa Makefile .
The sealed disk build runs
.Ql cfgcheck sealednet
and refuses to build a disk if the script and settings disagree.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/udhcpc.eth0.pid
.It Pa /etc/network/interfaces
Recovery's interface configuration, which starts the script.
.It Pa /var/run/udhcpc.eth0.pid
DHCP client's process ID.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1 -compact
.It 0
An address was already assigned, or the fixed address and route were set.
.It 1
The DHCP client would not stop, or the address or route could not be set.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
In the source tree:
.Dl tests/run drill
The suite boots recovery without a DHCP server and checks that eth0
has the fixed address and the DHCP client has stopped.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr busybox-networking 1 ,
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr dhcpc 8 ,
.Xr netup 8
